From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] user32: premultiply icon alpha like XP in the external shell

Purpose: draw 32-bit icons with XP's exact colours, as in the Alt+Tab
switch window.
XP behavior: DrawIconEx gives colour * alpha / 255, truncated, plus the
background as AlphaBlend gives it (tests/icon-alpha.c: 16 alpha by 16
colour values over five backgrounds).
Wine before: user32 rounded colour * alpha / 255 to the nearest value when
it made the alpha bitmap, one higher than XP in 104 of the 256 cases over
every background. The Alt+Tab window's folder icons differed from XP's by
one in 146 pixels.
Change: XP's rounding, as uxtheme-external-premultiply does for theme
images.
Evidence: tests/icon-alpha.c equals the reference XP machine's output.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL; the icon's owner and the drawing
process both run with it in the session (proxy, XP Explorer).
---
 dlls/user32/cursoricon.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/user32/cursoricon.c b/dlls/user32/cursoricon.c
index c9a5ef8..1a94b51 100644
--- a/dlls/user32/cursoricon.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/cursoricon.c
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 #include "controls.h"
 #include "wine/exception.h"
 #include "wine/debug.h"
+#include "wine/win4wine.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(cursor);
 WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(icon);
@@ -750,7 +751,18 @@ static HBITMAP create_alpha_bitmap( HBITMAP color, const BITMAPINFO *src_info, c
         }
     }
 
-    /* pre-multiply by alpha */
+    /* pre-multiply by alpha; XP truncates (tests/icon-alpha.c) */
+    if (win4wine_external_shell())
+    {
+        for (i = 0, ptr = bits; i < bm.bmWidth * bm.bmHeight; i++, ptr += 4)
+        {
+            unsigned int alpha = ptr[3];
+            ptr[0] = ptr[0] * alpha / 255;
+            ptr[1] = ptr[1] * alpha / 255;
+            ptr[2] = ptr[2] * alpha / 255;
+        }
+        goto done;
+    }
     for (i = 0, ptr = bits; i < bm.bmWidth * bm.bmHeight; i++, ptr += 4)
     {
         unsigned int alpha = ptr[3];
